  "notes": "The club-facing, synth-forward end of the TDE bench, and the research's one comparative claim is the parameter to hang the model on: **\"more fills than the Mustard template\"**, plus \"hand-clap doubling on hooks\" and \"32nd rolls into section boundaries\". Against a parent whose `hihat.rolls.freqPerBar` is 0.20 and whose `openHat.prob` is 0.55, this entry runs rolls at 0.35 — the top of the batch's allowed band — `fillDensity` 0.48, `openHat.perBar` up to 3, and percs at [2,4] and -5dB. Energy is the second parameter: \"forward, saturated 808 with short glides, kick-locked; the low end is the energy control\" is `distortion` `medium` at 0.35 wet with `portamentoMs` 30 and `bassline.followRootsProb` 0.86. Third, the melodies are \"catchier and more repeated than in the label's introspective material\" — `bright_bell`, `motifPitchCount` [3,5], `chordToneBias` 0.78, and 1-bar phrases weighted alongside 2. `session.keys` is authored to F minor and D♭ major/minor because that is the one measured fact in the entry. ⚠ `medium`, and the research is explicit: \"role, era and flagship credits documented; drum/harmony detail inferred from their placements **[LOW-CONF]**\" — so the `i–VI–VII` family and every drum number below are INFERRED from their principal artist's catalogue rather than from anything they said. ⚠ The 128-134 half-time population is not modeled (one `halfTime` boolean, no modes authored). ⚠ The \"stripped pre-hook\" is authored as a real `prechorus` section with its own `sectionBars` and `sectionRules` entry rather than as a drop-out, because the research names it as a section and the double hook that closes needs something to lean on. ⚠ **The 1-bar phrase length was removed** (was [1,2], now [2,4]). A one-bar phrase looped four times carries less entropy than a four-bar phrase, and it is the countermelody it strangles hardest: a counter answers *inside* the melody’s phrase, so a one-bar shape leaves it nowhere to go. Every worst offender on `counter.rs` carried it. ⛔ The previous session recorded this exact mistake and it arrived again from the other direction — distinctness is combinatorial in the shape LENGTH, not in the option count.",
